{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018pGSF79tYhupmgYfcgi1Eq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** This project stress-tests an AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator) by generating Go reimplementations of GNU utilities from formal SRDs, verified via differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline: extract (C source analysis) → specify (human-authored SRDs) → synthesize (orchestrator generates Go) → verify (differential testing via pkg/testutils). Shared libraries: pkg/sys (syscalls), pkg/format (output formatting), pkg/hashutil (hash computation), pkg/sizeparse (size parsing), pkg/encutil (encoding).\n\n**Current state:** 114 SRDs specified. Many releases fully implemented (01.2-02.2, 03.0, 05.3, 08.1). Generation run 44 is ongoing. Recent commits completed sha384sum (task 5501) and cksum R1.1-R1.4 (task 5500).\n\n**Current release:** Release 09.0 is the earliest release with \"ready\" requirements. sha224sum and sha384sum were recently completed; b2sum is already implemented. Remaining ready requirements: **srd077-cksum** R2.1-R3.3 (6 requirements) and **srd078-sum** R1.1-R3.3 (9 requirements).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 09.0 has two utilities with ready requirements: cksum (6 remaining) and sum (9 total). These are independent packages that can be worked in parallel.\n\n**Weight budget verification (all weights assumed default=1):**\n\n- Task 0: srd077 R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) + R2.3(1) + R3.1(1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 1: srd077 R3.2(1) + R3.3(1) = 2 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 2: srd078 R1.1(1) + R1.2(1) + R1.3(1) + R1.4(1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 3: srd078 R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) + R3.1(1) + R3.2(1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nCoverage: 14 of 15 ready requirements. srd078 R3.3 deferred to next batch.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/cksum implementation -- srd077 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd077-cksum.yaml (R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1 specifications)\n      - cmd/cksum/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R1.4)\n      - cmd/cksum/cksum_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/hashutil/ (shared hash utility library for algorithm support)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section for differential testing pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cksum/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality for srd077 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1\n      - path: cmd/cksum/cksum_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd077-cksum requirement R2.1 per the specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd077-cksum requirement R2.2 per the specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd077-cksum requirement R2.3 per the specification\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd077-cksum requirement R3.1 per the specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project convention\n      - id: D2\n        text: Follow the differential testing pattern from ARCHITECTURE.yaml shared_protocols -- use testutils.BuildBinary, exec.LookPath for gcksum, t.Skip if reference binary not found\n      - id: D3\n        text: Use pkg/hashutil for hash computation when algorithm selection requires standard hash algorithms\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./cmd/cksum/ succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go vet ./cmd/cksum/ reports no issues\n      - id: AC3\n        text: go test ./cmd/cksum/ -count=1 passes (both existing and new test cases)\n      - id: AC4\n        text: New differential test cases cover the functionality specified by R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1\n\n- index